<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippines' trade deficit widens to $7.133 bln.</title>
<headline>Philippines' trade deficit widens to $7.133 bln.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines' merchandise trade balance for the first seven months of 1996 stood at a deficit of $7.133 billion, a 46.3 percent rise over the $4.876 billion deficit in the same 1995 period, the government's National Statistics Office said on Friday.  </p>
<p> MERCHANDISE TRADE    Jan-Jul 96   Jan-Jun 96   Jan-July 95</p>
<p>    Exports		11.277	  9.583	 9.616</p>
<p>    Imports		18.410	 15.563	14.492</p>
<p>    Trade balance	-7.133	 -5.980	-4.876</p>
<p>Note - Figures are in billion U.S. dollars.  </p>
<p>The NSO said the trade deficit reached $1.144 billion in July alone, a 96.2 percent rise over the $583.0 million deficit recorded in July 1995.</p>
<p>    MERCHANDISE TRADE    July 96  Jun 96   July 95</p>
<p>    Exports		   1,694    1,793    1,592</p>
<p>    Imports		   2,837    2,738    2,175</p>
<p>    Trade balance	 - 1,144     -944     -583</p>
<p>Note - Figures in million U.S. dollars are rounded off.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom (632) 841-8900 Fax 817-6267</p>
</text>
